{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>If his master gives him a wife.</b> From here that the authority is in the master's hand to give him a Canaanite maidservant to beget slaves from her. Or is it not so, but rather an Israelite woman? Scripture says, ״the woman and her children shall be her master's״ — so it speaks only of a Canaanite, for the Hebrew woman also goes free at six — and even before six, if she developed signs, she goes free — as it says, ״your brother the Hebrew or the Hebrew woman״ (Deuteronomy 15), teaching that the Hebrew woman too goes free at six (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:25.871170304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}